From be6cd0f391384cbce844d9fc87b7ceb7988c5f63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:43:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Added: Send special keys from a panel of the extra keys
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A narrow, two rows tall ⊞ extra key right of Enter and Kbd opens a panel
of special keys above the extra keys, in 10 tabs: frequent keys (^C ^V
^X ^Z ^D ^A ^E ^L, F1 to F12, ^R ^W ^U Del), Ctrl, Fn, Edit, Alt,
Symbols, tmux, vim, nano and favorites. Tapping a key sends it like the
extra keys do, with Ctrl and Alt of the extra keys if they are on, and
closes the panel. A long press shows what the key sends and adds it to
or removes it from the favorites, which are kept in
~/.termux/special_keys_favorites.json and in the settings export.

Extra keys get the rows and width options for the key, like
{key: 'SPECIAL_KEYS', rows: 2, width: 0.5}.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GLNsTPnn2xKUQ4uFcevT6G
